    <!-- Power comes from this field and nowhere else. The engine derives
         supplies-made from living units that carry Food, so a device that is
         standing and online is counted automatically, per owning player, with
         no script involved. Disablement is a different unit type (below) that
         carries no Food, which is what makes the whole thing need no bookkeeping. -->
    <!-- No TerranBuildingBurnDown. It came along with the EngineeringBay this
         was copied from, and it is a second, undesigned failure mechanic: below
         a third of its life a Terran building takes 1 damage every 0.33s until
         it dies. On the downed variant that was fatal outright, since that one
         is born at 1 life and burned away in a third of a second. On this one
         it is subtler and worse for P0, a device chipped below a third would
         fail on its own with nothing attacking it, which is exactly the kind of
         unattributable event a greybox test cannot afford. Decay-if-unrepaired
         may be worth having later, as something chosen rather than inherited. -->
