            <LayoutButtons Row="0" Column="0"/>
            <LayoutButtons Row="0" Column="0"/>
            <LayoutButtons Row="0" Column="0"/>
        </CardLayouts>
        <EditorCategories value="ObjectType:Hero,ObjectFamily:Campaign"/>
    </CUnit>
    <!-- An employee.

         The individual the player sends to work an abnormality. Parented off
         Marine for the same reason the character is: everything not listed
         here is a Marine, so the entry reads as a diff.

         Unarmed. Training Team lv1 grants "npc文职人员也获得自卫武器", which
         only means anything if the default is no weapon; the department upgrade
         puts one back through an EffectArray row and needs no script.

         Light and Biological come off because they are risk grades here, not
         body types — see docs/dev/authoring-contract.md. An employee is not an
         abnormality.

         The four stats are the four veterancy behaviors below. Nothing in
         Galaxy stores a stat; 11_employee.galaxy only moves the XP.

         Permanent death is the absence of code, not a rule: nothing respawns
         these. That is deliberate (agents-and-abnormalities.md 2.6) and it is
         what Central Command's replenishment is priced against. -->
